What your weeks are going to look like

• Daily Scrum meetings;

• Build a trusted relationship with the partner by acting as the main point of contact within your area of expertise;

• Contribute to the various stages of design and development of a video game on a mobile platform within a multidisciplinary production team;

• Maintain smooth communication with other departments (design, art, production) to ensure optimal integration of all project components;

• Provide your expertise to determine the most appropriate technical approaches to achieve the desired project outcomes;

• Ensure code quality and adherence to development best practices (code reviews, testing, optimization);

• Mobilize, mentor, and support your direct team through ongoing coaching and continuous feedback;

• Collaborate with the Technical Director (Core Team) to ensure alignment with company standards.

In short, a leadership role where you remain hands-on technically, with evolving responsibilities, a stimulating mobile project, and FUN on a daily basis!
What we're looking for

• Bachelor’s degree in computer science or another related field combined with equivalent experience;

• Minimum of five (5) years of experience in development;

• Experience as a Lead Programmer or in a similar role;

• Strong command of the Unreal game engine;

• Excellent knowledge of C++ and strong optimization skills;

• Ability to travel abroad when required;

• Strong oral and written communication skills in both French and English. English proficiency is required, as we collaborate with English-speaking partners.

What we value in our team

• Demonstrated curiosity for new technologies;

• Strong team leadership skills;

• Ability to mobilize and mentor others;

• Excellent stress management in a fast-paced environment;

• Diplomacy, patience, resourcefulness, organization, and rigor.

Come and make a difference with us! #FrimaLife

